# Extracted from the published checkpoint by port/extract_reference.py; regenerate rather
# than commit (see "Weights" in README.md). weights.npz itself is 49 MB and is NOT tracked.
port/reference/
*.npz
__pycache__/

# The authors' TensorFlow checkpoint: 146 MB, two thirds of it Adam's optimizer slots, and
# over GitHub's 100 MB file limit. Neither it nor the weights inference needs (port/weights.npz,
# ignored by *.npz above) is in this repository; README.md, section "Weights", says how to
# regenerate them. To fetch the checkpoint back:
#     git remote add upstream https://gitlab.com/cheminfIBB/pafnucy
#     git fetch upstream && git checkout upstream/master -- results/
results/*.data-*

# local assistant settings: hold absolute paths from the machine they were written on
.claude/
